WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.120
The credits have rolled and&nbsp;
the reviews are in — but is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.840
Indy's final adventure whip-cracking&nbsp;
fun… or does it belong in a museum?

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:12.060
Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny has got&nbsp;
a lot riding on it. It's the first film in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.620
Indiana Jones franchise since Kingdom of the&nbsp;
Crystal Skull, which notoriously received a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:22.140
frosty reception from fans when it came out&nbsp;
in 2008. Dial of Destiny is also unique in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.160
that it's the first film in the franchise to&nbsp;
be neither directed by Steven Spielberg nor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.620
have a story by George Lucas. Top all of that&nbsp;
with a reported $300 million budget, and it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.820
clear that the pressure is high for Disney's&nbsp;
first — and maybe only — Indiana Jones project.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.260
Of course, a significant number of fans will&nbsp;
be happy just to see Harrison Ford suit up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.900
as Indy one last time, but nostalgia only goes&nbsp;
so far. The film has a June 30th release date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.100
in the United States, but, as it premiered at&nbsp;
the Cannes Film Festival, reviews have already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.080
begun trickling in. So what do critics have&nbsp;
to say so far about Indy's final adventure?

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.180
It's probably worth considering Dial of Destiny in&nbsp;
the context of the franchise's impressive legacy.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.740
"It's not the years, honey. It's the mileage."

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.700
Raiders of the Lost Ark is widely considered&nbsp;
one of the best adventure films of all time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.480
and people have plenty of love for&nbsp;
Temple of Doom and The Last Crusade, too.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.766
"Those people are trying to kill us!"

00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:16.540
"I know, Dad!" "

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.840
This is a new experience for me."

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.300
"Happens to me all the time."

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.980
While it's hard to say whether Dial of Destiny&nbsp;
will reach those heights, it certainly appears as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.060
though critics think the movie is a step up from&nbsp;
Kingdom of the Crystal Skull. More importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.080
many critics found it to be a fitting&nbsp;
conclusion to the Indiana Jones film saga.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.880
Fans can rest easy knowing the fifth installment&nbsp;
of the Indiana Jones franchise offers a fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.680
old-fashioned romp. GamesRadar+'s critic enjoyed&nbsp;
the throwback vibe of the movie, writing:

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.060
"There's a nostalgic, old-fashioned feel&nbsp;
to the film, a rollicking, globe-trotting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.680
ride that pits Ford's intrepid adventurer&nbsp;
against the Nazis once more. Certainly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.780
it makes up for 2008's outlandish Kingdom of&nbsp;
the Crystal Skull, with a more grounded story."

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.800
The final verdict from the outlet is&nbsp;
four out of five stars, with the summary:

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.340
"A terrific thrill ride. With Ford in fine form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.020
Indy's last stand is a highly satisfying&nbsp;
blend of action, humour and emotion."

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.060
Others agree the film is a lot of fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.740
with one mild criticism being that it&nbsp;
plays it too safe. The Radio Times says:

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:21.420
"Perhaps the film could've been more daring&nbsp;
– it feels fairly safe – but fans will leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.540
cinemas feeling like their old hero&nbsp;
had one final great outing in him."

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.060
While much of the focus is&nbsp;
naturally on Harrison Ford,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.200
the movie boasts a talented supporting&nbsp;
cast, including Phoebe Waller-Bridge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.400
And it sounds like she's more than a match&nbsp;
for Indy himself. As The Guardian notes:

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.620
"Phoebe Waller-Bridge has a tremendous co-star&nbsp;
turn as Indy's roguish goddaughter Helena Shaw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.240
who wears shorts and shirt making her look&nbsp;
like a grownup, naughty Enid Blyton heroine."

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.520
Meanwhile, the Radio Times praises how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.400
the film grapples with an aging&nbsp;
protagonist. The review reads:

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.320
"At its heart is a great performance from Ford,&nbsp;
one of his most emotional outings as Indy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.440
as he comes to terms with his&nbsp;
ageing body and life-regrets."

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.140
GamesRadar+ also notes how Indy's struggles with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.260
his age and regrets grounds&nbsp;
the movie. The review says:

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:09.000
"We see the character has grown older, but not&nbsp;
necessarily wiser. Drinking a bit too much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.440
he's full of regrets about pursuing fortune&nbsp;
and glory and leaving his loved ones behind."

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.520
Not every critic has been so enamored with&nbsp;
the movie, however. Donald Clarke of The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.960
Irish Times was a bit more critical, giving the&nbsp;
film three out of five stars and concluding that:

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.420
"Nobody with a brain in their heads will compare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.060
Dial of Destiny favourably&nbsp;
to the first three films."

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.800
But even if it's no Raiders of the Lost Ark,&nbsp;
it sounds like Dial of Destiny will see Indiana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:37.260
Jones go out swinging. At this point, even a solid&nbsp;
Indy adventure might be all anyone can hope for.

